it's virtually guaranteed that if you're  a superhero in the Marvel Cinematic  Universe your family is full of tragedy  even with the stiff competition from  folks like Thor and Peter Parker it's  hard to point out a super family with  more ongoing drama than the wakandan  royalty in Captain America Civil War  King t'chaka dies leaving his distraught  son to Chala seeking Vengeance in Black  Panther we find out that young tachaka  killed his exiled criminal brother in  jobu which sends the latter's son into  DACA on a path that turns him into  killmonger the movie's main antagonist I  found my daddy with Panther claws in his  chest you ain't the son of a king you're  a son of a murderer warning we're about  to get into Major Spoilers tell me the  spoiler's child and embrace your destiny  black panther wakanda forever doubles  down on the tragedy Trend in addition to  depicting t'challa's death a necessary  plot point to reflect the real world  death of star Chadwick Boseman Queen  ramonda also dies during during the  events of the movie after Queen  ramonda's Death it seems that t'challa's  younger sister shuri is the only  remaining member of her family leading  her down a path of violent Revenge from  which she veers away at the last minute  however the movie's mid-credits scene  actually reveals a new member of the  wakandan royal family we discover that  t'challa actually fathered a son with  Nakia as the latter introduces Sheree to  Young Tucson he reveals that his  wakandan name is in fact t'challa with a  name like that it seems like Marvel  Studios is setting the child up to  become a huge part of the MCU many years  down the line still major Marvel fans  might already have noticed that the MCU  origin of the character is quite  different from t'challa's son in the  pages of Marvel Comics bear his full  name is Azari t'challa and he's the son  of t'challa and storm a long time member  of the Axeman this version of the  character is actually from an alternate  future timeline from the mainline Marvel  Comics timeline Andy's a Teenage Mutant  who's inherited both his father's black  panther powers and his mother's power to  control lightning this of course is a  significantly different origin story  from the one wakanda forever's t'challa  Jr gets for starters he's still just a  small child when we meet him and we have  no idea whether he's inherited any of  the powers that were granted to his  father by wakanda's heart-shaped herb  though messing with a character's  background in live action adaptations  might annoy some fans it's  understandable that the MCU plays fast  and loose with t'challa's family tree  since storm hasn't been officially  introduced in the MCU and black panther  star Chadwick boseman's death in 2020  ended King t'challa's story there is no  way for the two to meet let alone start  a family meanwhile Nakia is t'challa's  former lover and obviously ongoing  romantic interest in Black Panther and  her linked the absence from the MCU  after the first Black Panther movie is  easily explained by the fact that she's  been in Haiti keeping the heir to a  Honda's Throne safe and hidden it's an  interesting move to introduce to  childless son at this exact point in the  MCU timeline not only does his existence  strongly hint that the Black Panther's  Legacy will continue even after shuri  but it also works wonders for her the  current black panther after all shuries  lost all the family members that she  knew of in relatively rapid succession  and is finally starting to resolve her  grief and Trauma by the time wakanda  forever ends the mid-credit scenes  Revelation that she's not the last  Living member of her family dovetails  perfectly with her character Arc of  accepting her losses and honoring her  family's Legacy black panther wakanda  forever is now in theaters  [Music]  foreign
 

